cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to LocalLeaf, please cite it together with Overleaf Community
  Edition, the software it is built on (listed under references).
type: software
title: "LocalLeaf: the Overleaf editor as an offline macOS application"
abstract: >-
  LocalLeaf is a modified version of Overleaf Community Edition. It packages
  Overleaf's LaTeX editor as a native macOS application that works on a local
  folder and compiles with the TeX distribution installed on the computer,
  without a server, an account or a network connection.
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Haixuan
repository-code: "https://github.com/HaiXuan-Lin/LocalLeaf"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
keywords:
  - LaTeX
  - editor
  - Overleaf
  - macOS
  - offline
references:
  - type: software
    title: Overleaf Community Edition
    authors:
      - name: Overleaf
        website: "https://www.overleaf.com"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/overleaf/overleaf"
    url: "https://www.overleaf.com"
    license: AGPL-3.0-only
    commit: e039ad26c5bf5422eb57b89fc7e57c75055e631d
    date-released: "2026-09-17"
    notes: >-
      The original work. LocalLeaf adds a local backend and packaging, and
      removes the features that need a server.
